inkedList`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In rare cases, if your type exposes a way to mutate the value of `T` through a `NonNull<T>`,"},{"DocComment":" and you need to prevent unsoundness from variance (for example, if `T` could be a reference"},{"DocComment":" with a shorter lifetime), you should add a field to make your type invariant, such as"},{"DocComment":" `PhantomData<Cell<T>>` or `PhantomData<&'a mut T>`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Example of a type that must be invariant:"},{"DocComment":" ```rust"},{"DocComment":" use std::cell::Cell;"},{"DocComment":" use std::marker::PhantomData;"},{"DocComment":" struct Invariant<T> {"},{"DocComment":"     ptr: std::ptr::NonNull<T>,"},{"DocComment":"     _invariant: PhantomData<Cell<T>>,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Notice that `NonNull<T>` has a `From` instance for `&T`. However, this does"},{"DocComment":" not change the fact that mutating through a (pointer derived from a) shared"},{"DocComment":" reference is undefined behavior unless the mutation happens inside an"},{"DocComment":" [`UnsafeCell<T>`]. The same goes for creating a mutable reference from a shared"},{"DocComment":" reference. When using this `From` instance without an `UnsafeCell<T>`,"},{"DocComment":" it is your responsibility to ensure that `as_mut` is never called, and `as_ptr`"},{"DocComment":" is never used for mutation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Layout"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `NonNull<T>` is guaranteed to have the same layout and bit validity as `*mut T`"},{"DocComment":" with the exception that a null pointer is invalid."},{"DocComment":" `Option<NonNull<T>>` is guaranteed to be ABI-compatible with `*mut T`, including in"},{"DocComment":" FFI."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Thanks to the [null pointer optimization],"},{"DocComment":" `NonNull<T>` and `Option<NonNull<T>>`"},{"DocComment":" are guaranteed to have the same size and alignment:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::ptr::NonNull;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<NonNull<i16>>(), size_of::<Option<NonNull<i16>>>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(align_of::<NonNull<i16>>(), align_of::<Option<NonNull<i16>>>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<NonNull<str>>(), size_of::<Option<NonNull<str>>>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(align_of::<NonNull<str>>(), align_of::<Option<NonNull<str>>>());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [covariant]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/subtyping.html"},{"DocComment":" [`PhantomData`]: crate::marker::PhantomData"},{"DocComment":" [`UnsafeCell<T>`]: crate::cell::UnsafeCell"},{"DocComment":" [null pointer optimization]: crate::option#representation"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":"NonNull","diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"src":"Normal","kind":{"Struct":[{"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":25,"beg":{"line":80,"col":4},"end":{"line":80,"col":52}},"generated_from_span":null}},"attr_info":{"attributes":[],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":false},"name":"pointer","is_positional":false,"ty":{"Value":[176,{"Pattern":[{"Value":[177,{"RawPtr":[{"Deduplicated":87},"Shared"]}]},"NotNull"]}]}}]},"layout":[{"key":"x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu","value":{"size":{"chosen":{"Deduplicated":24},"guarantee":{"Value":[650,{"Constant":{"Value":[293,[{"SizeOf":{"Deduplicated":176}},{"Deduplicated":0}]]}}]}},"align":{"chosen":{"Deduplicated":37},"guarantee":{"Value":[651,{"Constant":{"Value":[294,[{"AlignOf":{"Deduplicated":176}},{"Deduplicated":0}]]}}]}},"discriminator":{"Known":0},"inhabited":{"Deduplicated":0},"variant_layouts":[{"field_offsets":[{"guarantee":{"GuaranteedAlignment":{"Dedupl