r of **elements**, not the number of bytes."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This function is safe, but actually using the return value is unsafe."},{"DocComment":" See the documentation of [`slice::from_raw_parts`] for slice safety requirements."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`slice::from_raw_parts`]: crate::slice::from_raw_parts"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```rust"},{"DocComment":" use std::ptr;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // create a slice pointer when starting out with a pointer to the first element"},{"DocComment":" let x = [5, 6, 7];"},{"DocComment":" let raw_pointer = x.as_ptr();"},{"DocComment":" let slice = ptr::slice_from_raw_parts(raw_pointer, 3);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(unsafe { &*slice }[2], 7);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" You must ensure that the pointer is valid and not null before dereferencing"},{"DocComment":" the raw slice. A slice reference must never have a null pointer, even if it's empty."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```rust,should_panic"},{"DocComment":" use std::ptr;"},{"DocComment":" let danger: *const [u8] = ptr::slice_from_raw_parts(ptr::null(), 0);"},{"DocComment":" unsafe {"},{"DocComment":"     danger.as_ref().expect(\"references must not be null\");"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"ptr_slice_from_raw_parts","has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":68},{"Deduplicated":0}],"output":{"Deduplicated":80}},"src":"Normal","body":{"Structured":{"span":{"Value":[3289,{"data":{"file_id":18,"beg":{"line":1214,"col":0},"end":{"line":1216,"col":1}},"generat