 doing the shift in infinite precision"},{"DocComment":" then truncating as needed. Instead, the behaviour of this method matches what shift instructions"},{"DocComment":" do on many processors, and is what the `<<` operator does when overflow"},{"DocComment":" checks are disabled, but numerically it's weird.  Consider, instead,"},{"DocComment":" using [`Self::unbounded_shl`] which has nicer behaviour."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that this is *not* the same as a rotate-left; the"},{"DocComment":" RHS of a wrapping shift-left is restricted to the range"},{"DocComment":" of the type, rather than the bits shifted out of the LHS"},{"DocComment":" being returned to the other end. The primitive integer"},{"DocComment":" types all implement a [`rotate_left`](Self::rotate_left) function,"},{"DocComment":" which may be what you want instead."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(1_usize.wrapping_shl(7), 128);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(0b101_usize.wrapping_shl(0), 0b101);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(0b101_usize.wrapping_shl(1), 0b1010);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(0b101_usize.wrapping_shl(2), 0b10100);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(usize::MAX.wrapping_shl(2), usize::MAX - 3);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(42_usize.wrapping_shl(64), 42);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(42_usize.wrapping_shl(1).wrapping_shl(63), 0);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(1_usize.wrapping_shl(128), 1);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(5_usize.wrapping_shl(1025), 10);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":0},{"Deduplicated":42}],